---
// Home (site-prelaunch.md §2, v2.2 — ADR 0042 connection-led, #195).
// Deep door leads the hero sub; "Or, take any ticker" demo turn follows above the fold
// (demo-retention guardrail). Copy slots pending Growth #63 (site-copy-twiceover.md
// reconciliation per ADR 0042 pivot). Do not reword; layout must not change when #63 lands.
// COPY + STRUCTURE ONLY: "Connect read-only →" CTA and entry-box row stay RESERVED,
// not built (deferred to app-launch, #32); header sign-in slot reserved (Base.astro / §1).
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="TwiceOver — a second look at your own book"
  description="Connect your brokerage read-only and the read runs on the positions you actually hold — your rules, your horizons. Or take any ticker, no connection needed. Depth, never a verdict."
>
  {/* Hero — deep door leads the sub (ADR 0042, connect-led); demo retained above the fold.
      No pricing link in the reserved-box state: pricing via header nav + foot Pricing cue. */}
  <section class="hero">
    <h1 class="type-display">A second look at your own book.</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      Connect your brokerage <strong>read-only</strong> and the read runs on the positions
      you actually hold — measured against <strong>your own rules</strong>, across near-, mid-,
      and far-term horizons. <strong>Depth, never a verdict.</strong>
    </p>
    {/* Reserved — "Connect read-only →" quiet-outline CTA: built and wired to the app at
        launch (#32). No interim OAuth plumbing pre-launch. */}
    <p class="demo-turn">Or, take any ticker — no connection needed.</p>
    {/* Reserved — entry-box row (read-components.md §6, logged-out variant): built at
        app-launch (#32), wired straight to the app. No waitlist or interim capture path. */}
    <div class="connect-stages">
      <div class="stage-row">
        <span class="stage-chip">Any ticker · no connection</span>
        <span class="stage-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <span class="stage-chip">Your positions · your rules · your paths</span>
      </div>
      <span class="stage-engine">one engine</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wys" aria-labelledby="what-you-see">
    <h2 id="what-you-see" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">What you see</h2>

    <p class="group-label type-caption">On any ticker — no connection needed:</p>
    <ul class="what-grid">
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">The full read</h3>
        <p>the key technical levels, the macro backdrop and market regime, the curated voices of prominent traders, the options math and flow, fundamentals, and news and catalysts — each with its source and timestamp.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">One conditional, multi-horizon outlook</h3>
        <p>the evidence weighed into a near-, mid-, and far-term read, each stated as a condition ("while X holds…; a close below Y shifts the near read"). Labeled AI synthesis; every figure from the data pipeline, not the model. Never a score, never a "buy" or "sell."</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">A menu of structures, with the full math</h3>
        <p>the trades on that ticker, each with its complete numbers (net debit/credit, breakevens, max profit, max loss) and trigger levels. No ranking, no "do this."</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="group-label type-caption">Once you connect read-only — your own book:</p>
    <ul class="what-grid connected">
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Your structure, with the math <span class="tag">(connected)</span></h3>
        <p>your legs grouped into the position you actually hold, with net debit/credit, breakevens, max profit, max loss, and current P&amp;L.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Your rules, on live data <span class="tag">(connected)</span></h3>
        <p>the profit targets, DTE thresholds, and max-loss lines <em>you</em> configured, evaluated against where the position is right now.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Your paths, with the full math <span class="tag">(connected)</span></h3>
        <p>the moves available on what you hold, each with its complete numbers and trigger levels. No ranking, no "do this." The conclusion is yours.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
    <h2 id="how-it-works" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <p><span class="step-title">Analyze any ticker.</span> Type a ticker or ask in plain words. From licensed market and options data, TwiceOver synthesizes the key technical levels, the macro backdrop and market regime, the curated voices of prominent traders, and the options math and flow, all into one read — on any ticker, no broker connection required.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <p><span class="step-title">Connect read-only to make it yours</span> <span class="optional">(optional)</span>. Link your brokerage <strong>read-only</strong> and the same read runs on the positions you actually hold, measured against <strong>your own rules</strong>. TwiceOver can never place, change, or cancel an order, and never touches your funds.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="what-its-not">
    <h2 id="what-its-not" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">What TwiceOver is <em>not</em></h2>
    <div class="not-block">
      <p>Not an investment adviser. No recommendations, no trading signals, no scores, no ratings — and never a one-line verdict or a "buy" or "sell." It never executes trades and never holds your money. TwiceOver is a data-analytics tool that hands you the deepest read on a ticker — the evidence, the math, and the context — and leaves the decision where it belongs: with you.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="pricing-cue"><a href="/pricing">See plans</a> · <span class="muted">Launching soon.</span></p>
</Base>
